# referenceSystem - how git treats line endings (rev. 1.231).
#
# THE MANUAL PDF IS BINARY, AND GIT COULD NOT TELL. reportlab writes its
# streams ASCII85-encoded, so the file has no NUL byte and git's text heuristic
# took it for text. With core.autocrlf=true, a Windows checkout then rewrote its
# 334 LF bytes as CRLF, which moves every object the cross-reference table
# points at. Measured at rev. 1.231 on the committed rev. 1.222 manual: the blob
# reads cleanly, and the CRLF checkout of it makes pypdf report "incorrect
# startxref pointer" and fall back to reparsing. The blob in history was never
# damaged - it has no CRLF - only every Windows working copy of it.
*.pdf   binary

# POSIX sh refuses a CRLF script, and test/c/runStandaloneTests.sh is edited on
# Windows and run by CI on Linux.
*.sh    text eol=lf
